 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? The seat tube has sticker or marking showing the height. Lower it until the bottom bracket height is where it should be. No worries. Lower the seat until the bottom bracket is at the right height, then add a little spacer under the seat post if needed. That's usually the seat post length. You can either get a longer one and replace it, or lower the seat more with a spacer. Most people sit more forwards on the bike, so it' mostly about reach. If you can't touch the ground with your feet, a longer seat post is the",
